NMAE and NRMSE results for Table 1
Source: nmae_nrmse811.csv supplied and confirmed by the author as results from the completed experiments.
Evaluation: chronological 8:1:1 split; models: 11 baselines and MFTG-Net; forecast horizons: 24, 48, 72, and 96 hours.
Calculation: for each target channel f, s_f is the maximum absolute target value in the training split. NMAE is the mean of |y-y_hat|/s_f over channels and test forecast points; NRMSE is the square root of the mean of ((y-y_hat)/s_f)^2 over the same dimensions. Both are dimensionless ratios; multiply by 100 to obtain the percentage values shown in Table 1. Smaller values indicate lower channel-normalized error.
The source CSV contains one NMAE and one NRMSE value per model and horizon (48 records), without seed-wise values or standard deviations. The author confirms that the reported values are arithmetic means across seeds 2020, 2021, and 2022. Values below are transcribed as supplied, without recalculation.
